WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.660
Everyone knows about Elon Musk’s&nbsp;
companies, Tesla and SpaceX.&nbsp;

00:00:03.660 --> 00:00:09.720
But few know that he also co-founded OpenAI.
In the few short years of its existence,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:09.720 --> 00:00:15.060
OpenAI has become one of the world’s leading&nbsp;
artificial intelligence research labs.&nbsp;

00:00:15.060 --> 00:00:20.880
It ended 2022 with a bang….as millions&nbsp;
of people signed up for ChatGPT.&nbsp;

00:00:20.880 --> 00:00:26.340
Its question-and-answer computer program&nbsp;
is so popular that some schools have&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:26.340 --> 00:00:31.800
banned it to prevent students from cheating.&nbsp;
It took just one second to write me a poem about&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:31.800 --> 00:00:39.300
strawberry cheesecake in the tone of Shakespeare.
Another OpenAI tool generates art. I typed a few&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:39.300 --> 00:00:43.200
words, and DALL-E 2 produced&nbsp;
these beautiful designs.&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:43.200 --> 00:00:48.960
OpenAI’s futuristic research laboratory is housed&nbsp;
in this historic building in San Francisco.

00:00:48.960 --> 00:00:52.860
It's a small company with&nbsp;
only around 400 employees.&nbsp;

00:00:52.860 --> 00:00:58.620
But it's making huge advances in AI.&nbsp;
Everything it’s working on involves&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:58.620 --> 00:01:03.420
mimicking human intelligence by analyzing&nbsp;
tremendous amounts of data on the internet.&nbsp;

00:01:03.420 --> 00:01:07.980
The sheer amount of computing&nbsp;
required is incredibly expensive.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:07.980 --> 00:01:12.900
A professor in the University of Maryland’s&nbsp;
Computer Science department estimates&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:12.900 --> 00:01:19.320
ChatGPT costs $100,000 a day to run.
Some feel this estimate is far too low.&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:19.320 --> 00:01:24.780
AI has been touted as the next big thing for&nbsp;
a while now, but it wasn’t until recently that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:24.780 --> 00:01:31.440
the general public began taking it seriously.&nbsp;
OpenAI was only founded in 2015 as a non-profit&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:31.440 --> 00:01:37.380
platform by Musk and CEO Sam Altman.&nbsp;
Clip I think AI will be a technological&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:37.380 --> 00:01:41.100
revolution on the scale of the agricultural&nbsp;
or the industrial or computer revolution.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:41.100 --> 00:01:45.240
Before starting OpenAI, Altman was&nbsp;
the president of the venture capital&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:45.240 --> 00:01:50.940
company Y Combinator which helped launch&nbsp;
Airbnb, Reddit, Twitch, and many more.&nbsp;

00:01:51.480 --> 00:01:56.520
Altman and Musk teamed up with legendary&nbsp;
Silicon Valley investor Peter Thiel and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:56.520 --> 00:02:00.720
LinkedIn co-founder Reid Hoffman and&nbsp;
pledged $1 billion toward the project.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:00.720 --> 00:02:04.500
OpenAI’s current investors include Microsoft,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:04.500 --> 00:02:09.000
which is reportedly now investing&nbsp;
$10 billion into ChatGPT.&nbsp;

00:02:09.000 --> 00:02:16.860
Microsoft says it willl roll out ChatGPT on its&nbsp;
own AI service, Azure OpenAI. Companies like Al&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:16.860 --> 00:02:23.340
Jazeera use Azure for translation services. &nbsp;
Could ChatGPT breathe life into Microsoft’s&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:23.340 --> 00:02:27.000
struggling search engine Bing and&nbsp;
give Google a run for its money?&nbsp;

00:02:27.000 --> 00:02:30.240
Could it replace traditional&nbsp;
search engines altogether?&nbsp;

00:02:30.240 --> 00:02:36.840
Google CEO Sundar Pichai is supposedly taking&nbsp;
the threat seriously. He has reportedly told&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:36.840 --> 00:02:42.360
staff to focus urgently on developing&nbsp;
AI products.&nbsp;Google researchers revealed&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:42.360 --> 00:02:47.580
they were able to transform a few still&nbsp;
images into a 3D reconstruction of a scene.&nbsp;

00:02:48.240 --> 00:02:51.360
Google is competing against&nbsp;
a young and nimble company.&nbsp;

00:02:51.360 --> 00:02:56.640
This is what the first day at the office&nbsp;
looked like in early 2016. Pretty barebones.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:56.640 --> 00:03:00.600
The small team has come a long way,&nbsp;
but there’s still a long way to go.&nbsp;

00:03:00.600 --> 00:03:05.760
ChatGPT sometimes gives answers that&nbsp;
are misleading or downright wrong.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:05.760 --> 00:03:10.500
I asked it to solve this riddle:&nbsp;
Timothy’s mom has four sons. Their&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:10.500 --> 00:03:14.400
names are North, South, and East.&nbsp;
What's the name of the fourth son?&nbsp;

00:03:14.400 --> 00:03:21.600
ChatGPT says it’s West. But the answer is Timothy.
Altman warns that “it’s a mistake to be relying&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:21.600 --> 00:03:26.160
on it for anything important right now.”
But he does have high hopes and says future&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:26.160 --> 00:03:30.060
systems will make “ChatGPT&nbsp;
look like a boring toy.”&nbsp;

00:03:30.060 --> 00:03:34.560
The changes are coming fast.
OpenAI’s president tweeted:&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:34.560 --> 00:03:41.160
2023 will make 2022 look like a sleepy&nbsp;
year for AI advancement &amp; adoption.&nbsp;

00:03:41.160 --> 00:03:45.660
Musk responded to Greg Brockman&nbsp;
with a single word: Yikes.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:45.660 --> 00:03:50.760
There’s a lot packed into that word.&nbsp;
Musk has warned about the dangers of AI for years,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:50.760 --> 00:03:56.160
equating it to “summoning the demon.”
Here’s what he told CNBC in 2014.&nbsp;

00:03:56.160 --> 00:03:58.860
I'd like to just keep an eye on&nbsp;
what's going on with artificial&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:58.860 --> 00:04:04.260
intelligence. I think there's optentially&nbsp;
a dangerous outcome there. Dangerous?&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:05.340 --> 00:04:06.960
Potentially. How so?&nbsp;
I mean, there have been&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:06.960 --> 00:04:12.060
movies about this, you know, like “terminator”.&nbsp;
In the movie “terminator,” they didn’t expect,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:13.020 --> 00:04:18.660
you know some sort of Terminator-like outcome.&nbsp;
While Musk may be worried about advances in&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:18.660 --> 00:04:24.960
technology, ironically, his companies rely on AI.&nbsp;
Tesla is inching toward the full self-driving&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:24.960 --> 00:04:29.280
finish line thanks to AI.&nbsp;
Musk insists Tesla’s most valuable&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:29.280 --> 00:04:34.860
product ever could be its AI-powered bot.
His chip company Neuralink wants to sync&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:34.860 --> 00:04:39.900
the brain with artificial intelligence.&nbsp;
Musk resigned from the board of OpenAI&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:39.900 --> 00:04:45.360
to avoid any future conflicts because of&nbsp;
Tesla’s work in AI. He stayed on as a donor&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:45.360 --> 00:04:48.960
and advisor. (2018, three yrs later)
He insists he’s making sure AI is&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:48.960 --> 00:04:52.860
used for good, not evil.&nbsp;
OpenAI’s website states&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:52.860 --> 00:04:58.140
that its mission “is to ensure that artificial&nbsp;
general intelligence benefits all of humanity.”&nbsp;

00:04:58.140 --> 00:05:03.120
Artificial general intelligence is the&nbsp;
ability to learn any task that a human&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:03.120 --> 00:05:09.060
can so that faced with an unfamiliar task, an&nbsp;
AGI system can still figure out what to do.&nbsp;

00:05:09.060 --> 00:05:15.660
So what’s in store this year? Hey Alexa,&nbsp;
tell me what will happen in 2023.&nbsp;Sorry,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:15.660 --> 00:05:21.660
I can’t predict the future.Well, AI personal&nbsp;
assistants could get a lot smarter.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:21.660 --> 00:05:25.380
One prediction is that AI&nbsp;
will replace a lot of jobs.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:25.380 --> 00:05:31.380
Artists are already fearing for their livelihoods.&nbsp;
This AI-generated artwork even won an art&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:31.380 --> 00:05:36.780
competition in Colorado last year. (in 2022)
However,&nbsp; the World Economic Forum estimates AI&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:36.780 --> 00:05:42.360
will actually create millions more jobs than it&nbsp;
destroys, with high demand for machine learning&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:42.360 --> 00:05:46.440
specialists and data analysts.&nbsp;
As we look toward the future,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:46.440 --> 00:05:53.640
OpenAI’s next-generation version of ChatGPT is&nbsp;
highly anticipated and could appear in 2023.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:53.640 --> 00:06:00.240
And how about an AI that generates 3D models where&nbsp;
you type in a few words, and the program creates&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:00.240 --> 00:06:06.660
what usually takes animators hours to make?
OpenAI announced the 3D tool Point-E in a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:06.660 --> 00:06:12.420
research paper last year. It’s still a work in&nbsp;
process, and 2023 could see further developments.&nbsp;

00:06:13.080 --> 00:06:16.440
What OpenAI has shown is that a small dedicated&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:16.440 --> 00:06:21.060
team can change the world quickly.&nbsp;
Even if the road ahead is difficult.&nbsp;

00:06:21.900 --> 00:06:26.760
The CEO of OpenAI recently tweeted&nbsp;
about the importance of resilience.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:26.760 --> 00:06:29.100
Altman wrote:
“You’re supposed&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:29.100 --> 00:06:33.420
to pour your life force into something&nbsp;
and it’s not supposed to always be easy.”&nbsp;

00:06:34.260 --> 00:06:39.720
In the future, artificial intelligence will,&nbsp;
at the very least, make things look easy.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:40.740 --> 00:06:46.020
Despite the economic meltdown we all faced in&nbsp;
2022, it's clear there are still innovative&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:46.020 --> 00:06:52.200
companies on the rise. And while OpenAI is&nbsp;
showing promise, one unicorn fintech startup&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:52.200 --> 00:06:54.840
is delivering booming returns right now.&nbsp;
And the media is raving about it.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:54.840 --> 00:07:01.200
Masterworks has unlocked the potential&nbsp;
of contemporary art.&nbsp;A $1.7 trillion&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:01.200 --> 00:07:04.860
alternative investment that used to&nbsp;
only be available to billionaires.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:04.860 --> 00:07:10.800
With Masterworks, everyday investors can enter&nbsp;
the high-end art market without spending millions.&nbsp;

00:07:10.800 --> 00:07:14.100
Why art?
Contemporary art has outpaced&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:14.100 --> 00:07:21.540
the S&amp;P 500 by 131% over the last 26 years.
While the markets were getting crushed in&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:22.200 --> 00:07:28.500
2022…Masterworks saw 11 artworks deliver returns&nbsp;
to investors in the tens of millions of dollars.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:28.500 --> 00:07:35.220
Over 617,000 people have signed up&nbsp;
so far…including many of my viewers.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:35.220 --> 00:07:37.980
And you can sign up now to create a free,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:37.980 --> 00:07:40.680
no-obligation account at&nbsp;
the link in the description.

